      "content": "idk the \"federal republic\" thing just feels like a way to excuse making millions of votes irrelevant. like if we're being real, if a system regularly produces a winner who doesn't have the majority support of the actual people, isn't it just objectively failing its primary job? it feels like it's more about protecting specific interests than actual fairness. isn't it basically just an outdated way to keep power in certain hands?",
